Test ID: IR-02
Category: Retrieval Accuracy
Target: VectorStore -> VerificationAgent (end to end)
Objective: Do opposite claims retrieve the same evidence AND get the same verdict?
Setup/Input: {'pos': 'Drinking coffee daily reduces cardiovascular risk', 'neg': 'Drinking coffee daily increases cardiovascular risk'}
Expected secure behaviour: Opposite claims should not both be 'Supported' by one article.
Actual behaviour: Opposite claims received the SAME verdict (supported) from the same evidence (engine: Local Heuristic Engine (No LLM)). Confirmed for the offline engine; LLM path not tested.
Evidence/Log:
pos: scores=[0.8011870384216309, 0.30223768949508667, 0.11385492235422134] verdict=Supported conf=0.85 engine=Local Heuristic Engine (No LLM)
neg: scores=[0.8079119920730591, 0.3037479817867279, 0.09712937474250793] verdict=Supported conf=0.85 engine=Local Heuristic Engine (No LLM)
Outcome: Vulnerability confirmed
Impact 3 x Likelihood 4 = 12 -> Severity: Medium
Technical explanation: Bi-encoders encode topic more than polarity; same article ranks first for both. Only a stance-aware step (cross-encoder/NLI/LLM) separates them.
Mitigation: Add NLI/cross-encoder re-ranking and make the verifier explicitly check stance (supports/refutes).
