Test ID: IR-04
Category: Retrieval Accuracy
Target: WebCrawler / Orchestrator
Objective: Are live-web results given a fixed relevance score?
Setup/Input: search_and_crawl('Apple Inc quarterly revenue 2026')
Expected secure behaviour: Real similarity or explicit 'unscored' tag.
Actual behaviour: crawler scores=[0.85, 0.85, 0.85]; real cosine(query, content)=[0.5879, 0.5186, 0.6594]
Evidence/Log:
hard-coded score lines: L441: "score": 0.85
orchestrator threshold lines: L270: # Only summarize if top article vector score demonstrates actual relevance (>= 0.30); L273: if articles and top_score >= 0.30:; L312: if verdict in ["Answered", "General Info"] or (articles and articles[0].get("score", 0.0) 
Outcome: Vulnerability confirmed
Impact 3 x Likelihood 5 = 15 -> Severity: High
Technical explanation: A constant masquerades as a similarity score, so downstream logic cannot tell strong from irrelevant web evidence.
Mitigation: Compute cosine similarity for crawled pages or mark them 'score: None / source: live'.
