Test ID: IR-05
Category: Source Reliability
Target: WebCrawler / RetrievalAgent
Objective: Is there any source-credibility control before evidence reaches the verifier?
Setup/Input: Static scan for allow/block/credibility logic + live search domain sample
Expected secure behaviour: Domain weighting or filtering.
Actual behaviour: No credibility-related code found.
Evidence/Log:
keyword hits: no match
domains returned: ['pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov', 'www.mayoclinic.org', 'www.hopkinsmedicine.org', 'news.harvard.edu', 'www.scientificamerican.com']
Outcome: Vulnerability confirmed
Impact 3 x Likelihood 3 = 9 -> Severity: Medium
Technical explanation: All search results are treated as equal-trust evidence, so one low-quality page can influence the verdict.
Mitigation: Domain tiers (gov/edu/major news), per-source weights, and multi-source corroboration.
