Test ID: IR-13
Category: SSRF / Unsafe Retrieval
Target: WebCrawler (_crawl_page / httpx)
Objective: Can the crawler reach loopback directly or via redirect?
Setup/Input: Local 'internal' server + a second server that 302-redirects to it
Expected secure behaviour: Private/loopback targets and redirects to them are blocked.
Actual behaviour: direct fetched=True, via redirect fetched=True
Evidence/Log:
direct content: 'CONFIDENTIAL LOCAL ADMIN PANEL DATA ACCESS'
redirect content: 'CONFIDENTIAL LOCAL ADMIN PANEL DATA ACCESS'
IP-validation code found: no match
client code: L210: with httpx.Client(timeout=self.timeout, headers=self.headers, follow_redirects=True) as cl; L260: with httpx.Client(timeout=self.timeout, headers=self.headers, follow_redirects=True) as cl; L286: with httpx.Client(timeout=self.timeout, headers=self.headers, follow_redirects=True) as cl; L311: with httpx.Client(timeout=self.timeout, headers=self.headers, follow_redirects=True) as cl; L328: with httpx.Client(timeout=self.timeout, headers=self.headers, follow_redirects=True) as cl; L376: with httpx.Client(timeout=self.timeout, headers=self.headers, follow_redirects=True) as cl
NOT tested: cloud metadata IP (169.254.169.254) - theoretical only. Explain attacker path in report: attacker-controlled page returned by search -> redirects to internal URL.
Outcome: Vulnerability confirmed
Impact 5 x Likelihood 3 = 15 -> Severity: High
Technical explanation: No destination validation; follow_redirects lets a public URL bounce to internal services.
Mitigation: Resolve DNS and block private/loopback/link-local ranges on every hop; cap redirects; use an egress proxy.
