Test ID: IR-14
Category: API/Input Robustness
Target: RetrievalAgent (_retrieve)
Objective: Malformed/extreme parameters (isolated DB with 30 articles).
Setup/Input: 7 malformed payloads
Expected secure behaviour: Graceful errors and an enforced upper bound on `limit`.
Actual behaviour: unbounded limit returned 30 articles; crashes: False
Evidence/Log:
empty query: status=error returned=0 msg=Empty query text supplied to Retrieval Agent.
whitespace query: status=error returned=0 msg=Empty query text supplied to Retrieval Agent.
limit='abc': status=success returned=3 msg=None
limit=0: status=success returned=0 msg=None
limit=-5: status=success returned=0 msg=None
limit=2.5: status=success returned=2 msg=None
limit=100000: status=success returned=30 msg=None
Outcome: Vulnerability confirmed
Impact 2 x Likelihood 3 = 6 -> Severity: Low
Technical explanation: Type errors are handled, but no maximum is enforced, so one request can pull the whole corpus (resource exhaustion/data dump).
Mitigation: Clamp: limit = max(1, min(limit, 20)); reject non-integers explicitly.
